    "explanation": "Both sides end up agreeing that the SGD 4.00 cancellation fee cannot stand, and the recorded evidence shows why.\n\nThe driver's GPS trace (EV-GPS-09105, weight 1.0) holds 34 fixes from 13:05:00 to 13:10:30, every one at 0.0 km/h and 219.77 m from the Tower B pickup pin recorded in the trip record (EV-TRIP-09105, weight 1.0). This is a LARGE_VENUE pickup, so the POL-NS-02 arrival radius is 120 m. The driver never entered it: qualifying_fix_count is 0, longest qualifying in-geofence run is 0.0 seconds, and the minimum distance is 219.77 m, roughly 100 m outside the radius. POL-NS-01 limb (b) therefore fails outright, and the fee is not chargeable under that clause.\n\nThe case is the wrong-entrance situation POL-NS-03 governs, not a false-arrival case. The driver was stationary for the required 300-second dwell for this zone class — his trace spans about 330 seconds (13:05:00 to 13:10:30) — at a point outside the 120 m radius but well inside POL-NS-03's 400 m ceiling (219.77 m), so POL-NS-03 refunds the cancellation fee to the rider in full. On fault allocation, the rider named the correct sub-location in the chat log (EV-CHAT-09105, weight 1.0): 'I am at Tower B ride-hail pickup, beside the blue sign.' at 13:05:05 and 'That is the other entrance. Please come to Tower B.' at 13:06:35. The driver did not move to Tower B before cancelling at 13:10:30, and his own statement concedes he 'waited at a mall entrance for the full timer but did not move to Tower B.' POL-NS-03 limb (i) therefore puts the loss on the driver. No compensation and no pin-ambiguity goodwill (limb (ii)) is payable, notwithstanding the 3 registered pickup points recorded for this venue, because the rider specified the tower.\n\nNo false-arrival referral arises. The driver was stationary within POL-NS-05's own 300 m carve-out (219.77 m) at 0.0 km/h, and that clause expressly leaves a driver in his position to POL-NS-03; the 13:05:20 'arrived' marker therefore generates no POL-NS-05(ii) record and the referrals list is empty. The parties' remaining arguments do not change the result. POL-NS-06 points the same way (0-second in-geofence dwell against a 300-second minimum, a 300-second shortfall) but yields to POL-NS-03. POL-NS-04 is disputed but moot: the driver answered the 13:05:05 message 55 seconds later, yet left the rider's 13:06:35 request unanswered for the remaining 235 seconds — either way POL-NS-03 already refunds the fee in full with no compensation, so the clause decides nothing further. POL-NS-07's SGD 3.20 driver compensation does not arise because POL-NS-01 is not satisfied and POL-NS-03 displaces it; in any event the anti-farming check would not trip (no_show_terminations_30d of 1 against 120 completed trips in 30 days).\n\nOn the record's integrity: the missing traffic advisory (EV-ADVIS-09105-01, weight 0.0, issue MISSING_ARTIFACT) removes only POL-NS-06 limb (i), which is not needed here, and no POL-NS-08 limb is engaged — the trace has an empty gaps array and max_gap_sec 0.0 across 34 fixes, the chat log holds the 4 messages the trip record counts, the arrival marker lands on a fix timestamp with no skew, and the SGD 4.00 cancellation fee equals the greater of the LARGE_VENUE zone fee (SGD 4.00) and the RYDE_X vehicle-tier fee (SGD 4.00), so there is no POL-NS-08(d) fare defect. Every artifact carrying the deciding facts has weight 1.0, so confidence is not capped below 1.0, and no POL-NS-09 trigger fires: there is no unresolved contradiction, no second same-pair dispute (both counterparty counters are 0), no anti-farming pattern, and no abuse counter (rider no_show_disputes_30d is 0). The case is decided, not escalated, and the fee is refunded rather than held. Profile fields not named by a clause (prior_no_show_flags, prior_disputes_filed, ratings and the like) are context only under POL-GEN-01 and carry no adverse finding against either party.\n\nOutcome: the disputed SGD 4.00 cancellation fee is refunded to the rider in full; no driver compensation is payable.",
